{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P8CoveringE40lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCoverSay0G0QzGyF","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Covering\/ExactCovering.swift#L1739","fileName":"ExactCovering.swift"},"roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"name":"Covering","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Vertex","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"symbolKind":"method"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"It is the complement of the lexicographically greatest maximum independent set, not of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"least one: the least vertex of a symmetric difference is in one cover exactly when it is in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the other cover’s complement. That set is found as in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", with each choice the other way round: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"core pass on a bipartite component leaves out each vertex it decides, a complete component","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its greatest vertex, and any other component deletes a vertex whenever a maximum set","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"without it remains, with the reductions taking a simplicial vertex greater than all its","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"neighbours. The cost is that of ","type":"text"},{"code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": O(m √n) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"bipartite components, and up to c exponential searches on a component of c vertices the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reductions do not settle. The search does not check for task cancellation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph":{"title":"Graph","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph","fragments":[{"text":"extension","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P","text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Graph","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/Graph/Vertex":{"title":"Vertex","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/graph\/vertex","fragments":[{"text":"associatedtype","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Hashable","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Vertex","type":"topic","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering":{"title":"Covering","url":"\/documentation\/covering","role":"collection","abstract":[],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols/Graph/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols\/graph\/lexicographicallyfirstminimumvertexcover()","kind":"symbol","title":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover"},{"kind":"text","text":"() -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The lexicographically first minimum vertex cover: of the smallest vertex covers, the least"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"by vertex index (the rule of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"lexicographicallyFirstMaximumIndependentSet()"},{"type":"text","text":": of two covers"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of one size, the lesser holds the least vertex of their symmetric difference), in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"vertices"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order; [] for the empty graph. Every vertex with a self-loop is in it; parallel edges count"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"once."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/lexicographicallyFirstMinimumVertexCover()","role":"symbol"},"doc://Covering/documentation/Covering/GraphProtocols":{"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/covering\/graphprotocols","type":"topic","title":"GraphProtocols","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Covering\/documentation\/Covering\/GraphProtocols","abstract":[]}}}